{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The Fiedler vector: λ₂ and a unit eigenvector of it, with the canonical sign (see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"FiedlerVector","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"); nil when the graph is not connected. NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"fiedler_vector","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fiedlerVector","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalized","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":" = false, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":" = 1e-8) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FiedlerVector","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory13FiedlerVectorV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">? ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryInteger","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sz"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"normalized","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accepted when its residual is at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s (34 n from 5,000","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"solver.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Traps when the work limit is spent: 4,000 + 20√n products on σI − L (then shift-invert),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1,000 shift-invert products, 20,000 + 2n per solve. Only a tolerance below rounding has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reached it in the measurements.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"At least two vertices, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Every weight is finite and nonnegative.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Precondition"}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE13fiedlerVector6weight10normalized9toleranceAD07FiedlerF0VyxGSgqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_SbSdtSzRd__lF","remoteSource":{"fileName":"FiedlerVector.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector.swift#L193"},"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"SpectralGraphTheory"}],"title":"fiedlerVector(weight:normalized:tolerance:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fiedlerVector"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"normalized"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Fied